{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.SkeinFinitenessBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.SkeinFinitenessBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.particle_finiteness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.particle_finiteness","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.lean#L174-L188","doc":"The number of embeddable torus knots on genus 4 is finite (exactly 6). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bring_surface_torus_knots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bring_surface_torus_knots","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.lean#L157-L172","doc":"The Bring surface has genus 4.\nEmbeddable torus knots: (m-1)(n-1) ≤ 8.\nComplete list: T_{2,3}, T_{2,5}, T_{2,7}, T_{2,9}, T_{3,4}, T_{3,5}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.torusEmbeddable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.torusEmbeddable","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.lean#L151-L155","doc":"A torus knot T_{m,n} embeds in a surface of genus g\niff (m-1)(n-1)/2 ≤ g. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.pp_eigenvalue_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.pp_eigenvalue_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.lean#L114-L145","doc":"**Proven**: product of eigenvalues = det = −1 for the pp transfer\nmatrix (Vieta's formula).\n\nProof: `lam_p · lam_m = ((tr_T+√disc)(tr_T−√disc))/4 = (tr_T²−disc)/4`,\nand `tr_T² − disc = tr_T² − (tr_T² − 4·det_T) = 4·det_T = −4`,\ngiving `lam_p · lam_m = −1`. Uses `disc = ha² + 4 ≥ 0` so\n`(√disc)² = disc` via `Real.sq_sqrt`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.A_max_vanishes_strong_deformation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.A_max_vanishes_strong_deformation","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.lean#L102-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.A_max_vanishes_strong_deformation_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.A_max_vanishes_strong_deformation_axiom","kind":"axiom","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.lean#L95-L100","doc":"**External axiom (manuscript §6/skein-finiteness-bound):\nA_max vanishes as q → ∞.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.A_max_diverges_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.A_max_diverges_classical","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.lean#L91-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.A_max_diverges_classical_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.A_max_diverges_classical_axiom","kind":"axiom","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.lean#L85-L89","doc":"**External axiom (manuscript §6/skein-finiteness-bound):\nA_max diverges as q → 1⁺.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.A_max_approx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.A_max_approx","kind":"opaque","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.lean#L79-L83","doc":"The closed-form bound A_max(q) ~ π / √(4 ln q) — axiomatized as an\nopaque approximation function (its asymptotics are the content of the\ndivergence/vanishing axioms below). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.q_factorial_bounded_below_5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.q_factorial_bounded_below_5","kind":"axiom","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.lean#L74-L77","doc":"Below A = 5: [A-1]_q! ≤ [2]_q^{A-1}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.q_factorial_exceeds_at_5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.q_factorial_exceeds_at_5","kind":"axiom","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.lean#L67-L72","doc":"The critical condition: [A-1]_q! > [2]_q^{A-1}.\nAt A = 5: [4]_q! > [2]_q⁴ for q = 1.110. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.qFactorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.qFactorial","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.lean#L63-L65","doc":"The q-factorial [n]_q! = ∏_{k=1}^n [k]_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.qInt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.qInt","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.lean#L60-L61","doc":"The q-integer [n]_q = (q^n - q^{-n})/(q - q^{-1}). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IsStable.skein_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IsStable.skein_positive","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IsStable.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IsStable.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IsStable.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IsStable.mk","kind":"ctor","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IsStable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IsStable","kind":"structure","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.lean#L44-L49","doc":"A nuclear configuration (p,n) is stable at substrate parameter q\nif its Skein polynomial is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skeinPolynomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skeinPolynomial","kind":"opaque","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.lean#L35-L42","doc":"The Skein polynomial P(q) of N(p,n) — axiomatized as computed\nby the transfer matrix product ∏ V̂_i. ","signatureChunk":0}]}